26	/**
27	 * A {@link ClassOrderer} that orders {@link QuarkusTest}, {@link QuarkusIntegrationTest} and {@link QuarkusMainTest} classes
28	 * for minimum Quarkus
29	 * restarts by grouping them by their {@link TestProfile}, {@link WithTestResource}, and {@link QuarkusTestResource}
30	 * annotation(s).
31	 * <p/>
32	 * By default, Quarkus*Tests not using any profile come first, then classes using a profile (in groups) and then all other
33	 * non-Quarkus tests (e.g. plain unit tests).<br/>
34	 * Quarkus*Tests with {@linkplain WithTestResource#scope() matching resources} or
35	 * {@linkplain QuarkusTestResource#restrictToAnnotatedClass() restricted} {@code QuarkusTestResource} come
36	 * after tests with profiles and Quarkus*Tests with only unrestricted resources are handled like tests without a profile (come
37	 * first).
38	 * <p/>
39	 * Internally, ordering is based on prefixes that are prepended to a secondary order suffix (by default the fully qualified
40	 * name of the respective test class), with the fully qualified class name of the
41	 * {@link io.quarkus.test.junit.QuarkusTestProfile QuarkusTestProfile} as an infix (if present).
42	 * The default prefixes are defined by {@code DEFAULT_ORDER_PREFIX_*} and can be overridden in {@code application.properties}
43	 * via {@code CFGKEY_ORDER_PREFIX_*}, e.g. non-Quarkus tests can be run first (not last) by setting
44	 * {@link #CFGKEY_ORDER_PREFIX_NON_QUARKUS_TEST} to {@code 10_}.
45	 * <p/>
46	 * The secondary order suffix can be changed via {@value #CFGKEY_SECONDARY_ORDERER}, e.g. a value of
47	 * {@link org.junit.jupiter.api.ClassOrderer.Random org.junit.jupiter.api.ClassOrderer$Random} will order the test classes
48	 * within one group randomly instead by class name.
49	 * <p/>
50	 * {@link #getCustomOrderKey(ClassDescriptor, ClassOrdererContext)} can be overridden to provide a custom order number for a
51	 * given test class, e.g. based on {@link org.junit.jupiter.api.Tag} or something else.
52	 * <p/>
53	 * Limitations:
54	 * <ul>
55	 * <li>Only JUnit5 test classes are subject to ordering, e.g. ArchUnit test classes are not passed to this orderer.</li>
56	 * <li>This orderer does not handle {@link Nested} test classes.</li>
57	 * </ul>
58	 */
